  "before_edn": "{:db/id 17592186129282 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186128860 :question/id #uuid \"32f92fce-b4b9-5e7a-9fe0-255b15edf312\" :question/math-academy-id \"e-12417\" :question/problem \"Consider a small rectangle $\\\\Delta$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-1,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\\\delta{A}.$ Find an approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\\\mathbf T,$ given by\\n$$\\n\\\\mathbf{T}: \\n{\\\\left[ \\\\begin{array}{c}u \\\\\\\\ v\\\\end{array} \\\\right]} \\n\\\\longrightarrow \\n{\\\\left[ \\\\begin{array}{c}u {v}^{3} \\\\\\\\ {u}^{2} + {v}^{2}\\\\end{array} \\\\right]}?\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\textrm{Area}\\\\big(\\\\mathbf{T}(\\\\Delta)\\\\big) \\\\approx \\\\left| \\\\dfrac{\\\\partial (x, y)}{\\\\partial (u, v)} \\\\right| \\\\cdot \\\\underbrace{\\\\textrm{Area}(\\\\Delta)}_{\\\\large \\\\delta{A}}\\n$$\\n\\n \\n\\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\\\begin{vmatrix}\\\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\\\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\\\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\begin{vmatrix}{v}^{3} & 3u{v}^{2} \\\\\\\\ 2u & 2v\\\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\\\\  & ={v}^{3}\\\\cdot 2v-3u{v}^{2}\\\\cdot 2u \\\\\\\\  & =2{v}^{4}-6{u}^{2}{v}^{2} \\\\\\\\ {\\\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-1,2)} & =(2{v}^{4}-6{u}^{2}{v}^{2})\\\\,{|}_{u=-1\\\\,v=2} \\\\\\\\  & =2(2)^{4}-6(-1)^{2}(2)^{2} \\\\\\\\  & =32-24 \\\\\\\\  & =8\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, we have\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|8|\\\\cdot \\\\delta A \\\\\\\\  & =8\\\\,\\\\delta A.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid \"6d82be73-0720-5267-8698-427641b0e66e\" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186049035 :topic/difficulty 0.6172340118579578 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id 17592186429173 :encompassing/rationale \"Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account differential: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: differential=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/differential-frequency-estimates.json, pair 3706->1169. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json.\" :encompassing/topic {:db/id 17592186048857} :encompassing/weight 1.0} {:db/id 17592186429174 :encompassing/rationale \"Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account differential: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: differential=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/differential-frequency-estimates.json, pair 3706->1565. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relat